Give the last two custom colours their default

qtcDefaultSettings sets eight of the ten custom colours to black and
names neither customCrBgndColor nor customSortedLvColor. A file can name
a custom shade with no colour. The dialog can show the colour button of
the check mark background. Each path reads a QColor that no line of the
tree ever set.

The style holds its own Options and calls no default routine, so the two
fields hold a colour that reports itself as invalid.

Set both to black, the value that the eight sibling colours hold. The
render does not move, because an invalid colour already paints as black.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 10 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index 9ef6d216..fa594391 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -1740,6 +1740,8 @@ void qtcDefaultSettings(Options *opts)
     opts->customComboBtnColor.setRgb(0, 0, 0);
     opts->customMenuStripeColor.setRgb(0, 0, 0);
     opts->customProgressColor.setRgb(0, 0, 0);
+    opts->customCrBgndColor.setRgb(0, 0, 0);
+    opts->customSortedLvColor.setRgb(0, 0, 0);
     opts->titlebarAlignment=ALIGN_FULL_CENTER;
     opts->titlebarEffect=EFFECT_SHADOW;
     opts->centerTabText=false;
